+verify-san { dns:<name> | uri-hex:<hex> }
+  Adds a permitted TLS identity on a static "server" line. This option can be
+  repeated up to five times. Each value is at most 253 bytes. Use "ssl",
+  peer verification, and a "ca-file". Do not combine with "verifyhost" or
+  "verifyhost-strict".
+
+  At least one configured identity must match a subject alternative name of
+  the leaf certificate. A precise DNS name uses OpenSSL hostname matching
+  with full-label certificate wildcards only. A configured wildcard DNS
+  identity matches the same wildcard SAN only. URI values are the hexadecimal
+  encoding of the URI bytes and compare byte-for-byte. The configured "sni"
+  selects the certificate independently of its identity. Common names are
